   $q$What connection does the author draw in the final sentence of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Abernathy drew a map of the county to decide where to stop the truck.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The truck routes were later used as roads for the new branch libraries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The truck routes showed where readers were, which guided where branches were built.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The branch libraries replaced the trucks because the routes were too long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The truck routes showed where readers were, which guided where branches were built.$q$, $q$The county "placed them in the towns where the trucks had drawn the most readers," so the routes became "a map of where the county's readers lived." The word map is figurative, not a literal drawing.$q$, 'draft', '31a42254-5d03-5efd-85b2-b620d94fb34a')
