   $q$What happened first in Mwangi-Haro's discovery?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She taught the other village potters how to make green.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"She ran short of hardwood and burned pine and fence posts.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She added measured amounts of copper to her usual glaze.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"She learned that the old fence posts had been painted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She ran short of hardwood and burned pine and fence posts.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 begins the story with the shortage of hardwood and the substitute fuel. Learning about the paint and adding copper on purpose came later.$q$, 'draft', '4f90803e-61d5-522f-b155-61b684912c27')
